/**
@defgroup ghost The ghost
The ghost's AI, its states, its type and evidence, its senses and its footsteps. Concept pages:
[ghost AI](systems/ghost-ai.md) and [ghost types](systems/ghost-types.md).

@defgroup players Players
The investigators, each client's copy of them, and the input the game reads. Concept page: [players](systems/players.md).

@defgroup sanity Sanity
A player's sanity and what drains it. Concept page: [flames](systems/flames.md), "Sanity and Firelight".

@defgroup rooms Map and rooms
The level, its rooms and doors, its lights, its temperature and its flames. Concept pages: [flames](systems/flames.md)
and [doors](systems/doors.md).

@defgroup equipment Equipment
What players carry and what the level holds, and the evidence the equipment shows. Concept page: [evidence](systems/evidence.md), and
the [equipment guide](guides/equipment.md).

@defgroup weather Weather
A contract's weather and its lightning. Concept page: [weather](systems/weather.md).

@defgroup journal The journal
The journal's pages, ghost list and evidence, and the game's localised text. Concept page: [the journal](systems/journal.md).

@defgroup voice Voice chat
Each player's voice, how to read it and who hears whom. Concept page: [voice chat](systems/voice.md).

@defgroup lobby Lobby, contract and network
Rooms and who is in them, a contract's start and end, the difficulty and the menus. Concept pages:
[Photon](systems/photon.md), [the contract](systems/contract.md), [the difficulty](systems/difficulty.md) and [the menus](systems/menus.md).

@defgroup content Content and the host contract
Registering ghosts and evidence, rules on a ghost type, and the contract a mod's DLL has with the host. Guides:
[adding a ghost](guides/adding-a-ghost.md) and [adding evidence](guides/adding-evidence.md).

@defgroup runtime The runtime and Unity
Reaching the game through the map: typed entries, hooks, keeping objects alive, and the Unity types the game uses. See
[the SDK's README](README.md), and [navigation](systems/navigation.md) for routes over the level's navigation mesh.
*/
